  {
   "say": "Here's what nobody tells you.",
   "cap": "HERE'S WHAT | *NOBODY* TELLS YOU.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Most condoms already come with lube in the wrapper.",
   "cap": "MOST CONDOMS | ALREADY COME WITH | *LUBE* IN THE WRAPPER.",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Adding more is fine. It can even help stop them breaking.",
   "cap": "ADDING MORE IS *FINE.* | IT CAN EVEN HELP | STOP THEM *BREAKING.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "But only the right kind.",
   "cap": "BUT ONLY | THE *RIGHT KIND.*",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Water based or silicone lube. Both safe.",
   "cap": "WATER-BASED | OR *SILICONE* LUBE. | BOTH *SAFE.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Oil is the problem.",
   "cap": "*OIL* IS THE PROBLEM.",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "In one lab test, sixty seconds of mineral oil cut condom strength by about ninety percent.",
   "cap": "IN ONE LAB TEST, | *60 SECONDS* | OF MINERAL OIL | CUT CONDOM STRENGTH | BY ABOUT *90%.*",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "And mineral oil is in baby oil, and lots of lotions.",
   "cap": "MINERAL OIL IS IN | *BABY OIL,* AND | LOTS OF *LOTIONS.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "So with latex condoms: no Vaseline, no lotion, no coconut oil.",
   "cap": "WITH LATEX CONDOMS: | NO *VASELINE,* | NO *LOTION,* | NO *COCONUT OIL.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "The condom already brought its own lube.",
   "cap": "THE CONDOM ALREADY | BROUGHT ITS *OWN LUBE.*",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Let it do its job.",
   "cap": "LET IT | *DO ITS JOB.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Follow,",
   "cap": "*FOLLOW*",
   "pause": 0.15
  },
  {
